## 6. Termination

1. An Approved Contributor's status, and all rights granted under Section 2,
   terminate automatically when the person ceases to hold an active
   collaborator or maintainer role on the GitHub repository, whether by removal
   or by the Licensor's deletion or transfer of the repository.
2. Upon termination, the former Approved Contributor must:
   a. immediately cease all distribution of the Software;
   b. within thirty (30) days, delete all copies of the source code and derived
      material from systems under their control, except one archival copy that
      may be retained solely for personal records and may not be used,
      distributed, or disclosed in any way; and
   c. continue to be bound by Section 4 (Restrictions) with respect to all
      information and material obtained while an Approved Contributor.
3. Termination of an individual's contributor status does not terminate the
   rights of End Users who legitimately received prebuilt copies before
   termination, provided they comply with Section 3.

